 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bekhorot.29a.10",
   "daf": "29a",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: לָא קַשְׁיָא — כָּאן בִּשְׂכַר הֲבָאָה וּמִלּוּי, כָּאן בִּשְׂכַר הַזָּאָה וְקִידּוּשׁ.",
   "en": "«Abaye said:» This is «not difficult,» since «there,» the mishna in Kiddushin is referring to one who betroths a woman «with» the value of «the payment for bringing» the ashes from afar «and filling» the vessel with the purification water, for which it is permitted to accept payment. Performing this act for the woman is comparable to giving her an item of value, since she will not have to pay someone to bring and fill the vessel for her. «Here,» the mishna is referring «to payment for» the actual «sprinkling and sanctifying» of the ashes."
  },
  {
   "id": "bekhorot.29a.11",
   "daf": "29a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "דַּיְקָא נָמֵי, דְּקָתָנֵי הָכָא ״לְהַזּוֹת וּלְקַדֵּשׁ״, וְהָתָם קָתָנֵי ״הַמְקַדֵּשׁ בְּמֵי חַטָּאת וּבְאֵפֶר חַטָּאת״, שְׁמַע מִינַּהּ.",
   "en": "The Gemara comments: According to this answer, the language of the two mishnayot is «also precise, as it teaches here: To sprinkle, or: To sanctify,» indicating that he receives payment for the actual sprinkling and sanctification; «and it teaches there,» in the mishna in Kiddushin, that she is betrothed «with the water of purification or with the ashes of purification,» which indicates that the water and ashes have not yet been mixed together. The Gemara affirms: «Learn from it» that this is the correct explanation of the mishnayot."
  }
 ],
